{"id": "tea:unmai-vilakkam:36", "source": "src:unmai-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "36"}, "paraphrase": "The dance of the Lord is the five acts: creation from the drum, protection from the hand that grants fearlessness, destruction from the fire, concealment from the planted foot, and release (grace) from the raised foot.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:dance-of-nataraja", "cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "terms": ["trm:ananda-tandava", "trm:pancakrtya"], "notes": "Verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:unmai-vilakkam:pancaksara-section", "source": "src:unmai-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "pancaksara-section"}, "paraphrase": "In the five letters na-ma-śi-vā-ya, 'na' is concealment (tirōtam), 'ma' is mala, 'śi' is Śiva, 'vā' is his grace (aruḷ) and 'ya' is the soul; the soul standing between mala and Śiva should turn toward grace; placing 'śi' first (śivāya nama) is the subtle form.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:pancaksara"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancaksara"], "practices": ["prc:pancaksara-japa"], "notes": "Section-level reference; the letter correspondences are recalled with moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:unmai-vilakkam:tattva-section", "source": "src:unmai-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "tattva-section"}, "paraphrase": "The body and world are made of thirty-six tattvas: twenty-four of the soul (ātma-tattva: the elements, subtle elements, organs and inner organs), seven of knowledge (vidyā-tattva: māyā, kalā, kāla, niyati, vidyā, rāga, puruṣa) and five of Śiva (śiva-tattva); the soul must know them as not itself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:thirty-six-tattvas"], "terms": ["trm:tattva"], "notes": "Section-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
